<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15032" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρί-ζηλος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span> (
			Dor.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ζηλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					9(1).270
				</span></i>
			), also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, v. infr.:—
				Ep.
			 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρίδηλος </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ζηλος</span> from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ</span><i>y</i><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ηλος</span>, cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆλος</span> from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δε</span><i>y</i><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αλος</span> and
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέατο</span>), <i>conspicuous,</i>
			of lightning, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρίζηλοι δέ οἱ αὐγαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.244
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				2.61
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i><i>lchn.</i><i><span class="en">
				72
			</span></i>; of sound, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς δ᾽ ὅτ᾽ ἀριζήλη φωνή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					18.219
				</span></i>
			; of persons whom all admire, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥς τε
				θεώ περ ἀμφὶς ἀριζήλω</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				519
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				4.1.3
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>), etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥεῖα δ᾽ ἀρίζηλον μινύθει καὶ ἄδηλον
					ἀέξει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀριζήλως, εἰρημένα</span> a
			<i>plain</i> tale, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				12.453
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Dor.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρίζαλος </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῆλος</span>), = sq., <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Epigr.</u>
				52
			</span></i>, Hsch.s.v.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρι-.</span></div>
